=== layout: section

# Quiz

=== layout: two-panels

# *Quiz System Information*

@left

- 20 points; 18-24 questions
- MC\: 1 point; matching\: 1/2 per choice
- 30 minutes; about 1.5 min/question
- Backtracking allowed; random order
- Limited calculations
- Score\: (individual + group)/2
- Example\: (14 + 20)/2 = 17

@right

- Individual\: Blackboard
- Opens >20 hours before class
- Due BEFORE class
- Group\: Zoom and Blackboard
- 3-4 students; breakout setup takes time
- Hard group quizzes receive a curve

=== layout: one-panel

# *Missing Group Quizzes*

@body

- Make-up quizzes will be allowed for full credit only if the student notifies the instructor BEFORE the quiz/exam
- Students missing group quizzes cannot later work in a group
  - the individual score will be averaged with the minimum 18 points (or higher) instead of a group quiz score
  - so you still get the benefit of the group score average, albeit small, even though you missed the in-class quiz.

=== layout: one-panel

# *Low Quiz Grades*

@body

- How can I do better in this class?
- Did you complete the relevant assignments before taking the quiz?
  - The assignments and quizzes mostly have the same questions.
- Did you retake the relevant assignments and make sure you understood the questions? Did you retake them until you had a grade you were happy with?
  - The assignments and quizzes mostly have the same questions.

